-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",143,{
[4545]="70017527\n1\tHelp Ymar to control disease in Skûmfil\030Help Odmar defeat the kergrim-leaders of Skûmfil\030Help Glorelloth collect samples in Skûmfil\tYmar, Odmar, and Glorelloth are at the Shadowed Refuge. Throstur informed you that the kergrim within Skûmfil are eaters of the dead. As such, they are also rife with disease and filth, and he has set his agents to the task of deciphering what ills the kergrim carry through Skûmfil.\n2\tTalk to Throstur at the Shadowed Refuge\tThrostur is at the Shadowed Refuge. You completed each task assigned by Ymar, Odmar and Glorelloth within Skûmfil and should now return to Throstur.\n",
[4546]="7002C5A3\n1\tSlay Gripjaw\030Slay Dread-gaze\tGripjaw and Dreadgaze are in the foetid caves. You should defeat the two vilest hounds of all.\n2\tTalk to Sabert\tSabert is at the gate of Stangard. You should speak with Sabert of the two vile hounds you encountered in the foetid caves.\n",
[4547]="7002EFE9\n1\tTalk to Hutha\tHutha is standing near Burnoth outside the Mead Hall of Eaworth. Burnoth asked you to give Hutha his instructions, then return to him.\n2\tTalk to Burnoth to begin preparations for the siege of Eaworth\tBurnoth is standing outside the Mead Hall of Eaworth. You should speak with Burnoth when you are prepared to join the defence of Eaworth.\n3\tTalk to Burnoth outside the Mead Hall of Eaworth\tBurnoth stands outside the Mead Hall of Eaworth. You should return to Burnoth and discuss your victory.\n",
[4548]="700017DC\n1\tIntroduce yourself to Colbert the Mad\tColbert the Mad is at Mincham's Camp at the south-west edge of the Fields of Fornost. You should introduce yourself to Colbert the Mad.\n2\tSpeak with Mincham\tMincham is at Mincham's Camp at the south-west edge of the Fields of Fornost. You should speak with Mincham.\n3\tIntroduce yourself to Idhremmin\tIdhremmin is at Mincham's Camp at the south-west edge of the Fields of Fornost. You should introduce yourself to Idhremmin.\n",
[4549]="70017589\n1\tDefeat Snapjaw in the Redhorn Lodes\030Acquire musical text from Snapjaw's corpse\tThe deep-claw Snapjaw can be found in the Redhorn Lodes south-west of the bridge that crosses the crevace south of the Broken Stair. Snapjaw has been rumoured to hoard a great deal of paper-scraps and texts, undoubtedly some of great historic value, to build nests for its brood. Pada wishes you to recover a sheet of music that can likely be taken from Snapjaw upon its defeat.\n2\tBring the texts to Pada\tPada is in the Foundations of Stone, east from the Redhorn Lodes and then south to the Shadowed Refuge. You should return to Pada with the musical text you have found, and hopefully it will be the one that he is seeking.\n",
[4550]="7004D700\n1\tRetrieve wine (total: 7)\tWine can be found within Felegoth's wine cellar. You should fetch some wine.\n2\tWood Elves can be found in Felegoth. You should give wine to Elves within Felegoth.\t\n3\tUse dance near Galion\030Use dance near Hithlos\030Use dance near Wood Elf\tMany Elves live within the halls of Felegoth. You should dance with some of the Elves.\n4\tTalk to Hithlos\tHithlos can be found in Felegoth. You should talk to Hithlos.\n",
[4551]="7005FA4C\n1\tRealign echo-horns to unsettle the Orcs at Drúkala (total: 7)\tEcho-horns can be found in and around Drúkala in Gloomingtarn. Since learning that the Orcs fear the strange echoes in Gloomingtarn, Spall has asked you to realign the echo-horns at Drúkala in an effort to drive the Orcs back into Deepscrave.\n2\tCompleted\tYou have done as Spall requested and realigned the echo-horns at and around Drúkala.\n",
[4552]="700490DD\n1\tDefeat Sapakár\tSapakár can be found somewhere in Barad-dûr. You should confront Sapakár.\n2\tLook\tYou should look over the edge into the abyss of Mordath.\n3\tTalk to Lômazar\tLômazar can be found at the Ruins of Díngarth. You should speak with Lômazar.\n",
[4553]="700385D0\n1\tSpeak with Saburg\tSaburg is by your side. You should speak with Saburg.\n2\tHead east\tThe fox wants you to run north-east, up the small hill near his den. You should follow the fox and run east.\n3\tFollow the fox north\tThe fox wants you to run north. You should follow the fox and run north.\n4\tExamine the fox\tThe fox is by your side. You should examine the fox.\n5\tSee if Saburg is satisfied that her fox will not suffer without her\tSaburg is by your side. You should speak with Saburg.\n6\tBring Saburg to Cyneswith\tCyneswith is in Edoras, waiting for her daughter to come home. You should bring Saburg to her mother Cyneswith.\n7\tSpeak with Saburg at your side\tSaburg is by your side. You should speak with Saburg.\n8\tReturn to Théolac\tThéolac is on the platform in western Edoras. You should return to Théolac and tell him that the missing girl has been found.\n",
[4554]="7003A23F\n1\tPick up the food and carry it to Éowyn's room\tÉowyn's serving of food can be found on a table near the throne of Meduseld. Her room is to the left of the throne. You should bring Éowyn's food to her room to await her.\n2\tÉowyn's room is in Meduseld. You should examine Éowyn's room for signs that Witwyn is correct about the Lady's gloomy mood.\t\n3\tReturn to Witwyn\tWitwyn is in Meduseld. You should speak with Witwyn.\n",
[4555]="700397C0\n1\tEnter the disputed house\tThe disputed estate can be found atop a hill near the fountain north of Meduseld in Edoras. You should enter the estate and have a look around.\n2\tThere are messes all over the house, untouched from when Sigun and Sigmar's father passed away. A lovely house such as this should not go to ruin when two able men stand outside quarrelling. You should clean the house.\t\n3\tCompleted\tYou have scoured some of the old messes in the abandoned home, and it begins to look better already.\n",
[4556]="700385A5\n1\tLook around the second and third floors\tThe second and third floors can be found in Meduseld, the great hall in Edoras. You should climb the stairs to the higher floors and have a last look around.\n2\tExamine the loose floorboard\tThe loose floorboard can be found on the third floor of Meduseld. You should examine the loose floorboard.\n3\tBring the letter to Éowyn\tÉowyn stands on the steps of Meduseld, looking out upon Edoras. You have found an opened letter in the loose floorboards in Meduseld, and should bring it to Éowyn at once.\n",
[4557]="700385D1\n1\tAsk Cyneswith about her missing daughter\tCyneswyth can be found outside of her home in western Edoras. You should ask Cyneswith about her missing daughter.\n2\tAsk the neighbours if they have seen Saburg\tThe neighbours can be found next to Cyneswith home in western Edoras. You should ask the neighbours if they have any knowledge of Saburg's whereabouts.\n3\tSaburg's neighbour mentioned that Saburg often returned home with scrapes, covered in dirt and brambles. You should check the rocky outcroppings outside the eastern wall of Edoras for signs of Saburg.\t\n4\tSpeak with Saburg\tSaburg can be found amongst the rocks just outside the south-east corner of Edoras. You should urge Saburg to hurry home to her mother.\n",
[4558]="700385A3\n1\tMesses can be found on the tables throughout Meduseld, the great hall of Edoras in Kingstead. You should clean up messes left by the king's departure feast.\t\n2\tSpeak with Witwyn\tWitwyn is in Meduseld, the great hall of Edoras in Kingstead. You should speak with Witwyn.\n",
[4559]="700385A4\n1\tTapestries line the walls of Meduseld in Edoras. You should examine the tapestries.\t\n2\tCompleted\tYou have examined the magnificent tapestries lining the halls of Meduseld depicting the history of Rohan.\n",
[4560]="7003A099\n1\tWater crops one last time (total: 5)\030Pull the last of the weeds (total: 5)\tFrantic gardeners and farmers can be found throughout the eastern side of Edoras, where poorer townspeople rely upon their crops. You should help the frantic gardeners and farmers tend their plots.\n2\tSpeak with Léodferth\tLéodferth can be found near the east gate of Edoras. You should speak with Léodferth.\n",
[4561]="7003A2B1\n1\tTry to cheer Éowyn\tÉowyn stands outside of Meduseld, looking out upon Edoras. You should speak with Éowyn.\n2\tSpeak with Éowyn\tÉowyn stands outside of Meduseld, looking out upon Edoras. You should speak with Éowyn.\n",
[4562]="70038280\n1\tObserve Éowyn's meeting with her stewards\tÉowyn sits upon the king's seat in Meduseld. You should observe the lady's meeting with her stewards.\n2\tOffer your assistance to Éowyn\tÉowyn can be found standing outside of Meduseld, looking out over Edoras. You should speak with Éowyn to find out how you can help aid in moving the city.\n",
[4563]="700385A2\n1\tOffer help to Britred\030Offer help to Théolac\030Offer help to Léodferth\tLéodferth, Britred, and Théolac can be found throughout Edoras. You should speak with each of the three stewards and help them.\n2\tSpeak with Éowyn\tÉowyn can be found near Meduseld, looking out over the city. You should return to Éowyn.\n3\tSpeak with Witwyn\tWitwyn is inside Meduseld in Edoras. You should speak with Witwyn.\n",
[4564]="700399AF\n1\tMelancholic people can be found in and near the market square in northern Edoras. You should search the town for melancholic people and find out what is bothering them.\t\n2\tSearch for the Minstrel of Edoras\tThe town Minstrel seems to be sharing sad lines of poetry and song with the townsfolk, making them inconsolable. He can likely be found at the tavern of Edoras. You should speak with the Minstrel of Edoras.\n",
[4565]="700395C1\n1\tSearch for Dúdrad by the river\tDúdrad can likely be found by the river running to the west of Edoras. You should search for Dúdrad and encourage him to return.\n2\tFish alongside Dúdrad (total: 6)\tDúdrad's fishing area can be found where the river meets the road, just outside of the south-east wall of Edoras. You should fish with Dúdrad so that he is not alone in his last fishing routine before leaving his home behind.\n3\tSpeak with Dúdrad\tDúdrad's fishing area can be found where the river meets the road, just outside of the south-west wall of Edoras. You should speak with Dúdrad.\n",
[4566]="70039825\n1\tSearch the desk\tYou find a messy desk in Signoth's estate. You should examine the contents of the desk.\n2\tRead the note you found\tYou have found a note. You should read the note.\n3\tFind the second clue mentioned in Signoth's letter\tThe abandoned house in Edoras can be found north of Meduseld. You should search the house for clues based on Signoth's letter.\n4\tExamine the tapestry\tThe abandoned house in Edoras can be found north of Meduseld. You should search the house for clues based on Signoth's letter.\n5\tRead the note you found\tYou have found a note. You should read the note.\n6\tFind the third clue mentioned in Signoth's letter\tThe abandoned house in Edoras can be found north of Meduseld. You should search the house for clues based on Signoth's letter.\n7\tExamine the table setting\tThe abandoned house in Edoras can be found north of Meduseld. You should search the house for clues based on Signoth's letter.\n8\tRead the note you found\tYou have found a note. You should read the note.\n9\tFind the last clue mentioned in Signoth's letter\tThe abandoned house in Edoras can be found north of Meduseld. You should search the house for clues based on Signoth's letter.\n10\tExamine the bed\tThe abandoned house in Edoras can be found north of Meduseld. You should search the house for clues based on Signoth's letter.\n11\tRead the note you found\tYou have found a note. You should read the note you found.\n12\tSearch the lockbox\tThe lockbox containing the true deed to the house can be found at the foot of the bed. You should open the lockbox.\n13\tRead the deed and bring the documents to Britred\tBritred can be found on the wall above the fountain in northern Edoras. You should bring the deed to Britred.\n14\tTell Sigun that he has lost his claim on the house\030Tell Sigmar that he has lost his claim on the house\tThe two brothers, Sigun and Sigmar, can be found outside their home in northern Edoras. You should tell the two brothers that they have lost their claim on their father's house.\n15\tCompleted\tYou have reconciled the brothers by taking away that which they fought over.\n",
[4567]="7003983E\n1\tChoose the first colour\tThe lockbox is in Signoth's estate in Edoras. You should open the lockbox by choosing the correct colour. NOTE: From left to right, the gems are Blue, Green, Red, Purple. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tChoose the second colour\tThe lockbox is in Signoth's estate in Edoras. You should open the lockbox by choosing the correct colour. NOTE: From left to right, the gems are Blue, Green, Red, Purple. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tChoose the third colour\tThe lockbox is in Signoth's estate in Edoras. You should open the lockbox by choosing the correct colour. NOTE: From left to right, the gems are Blue, Green, Red, Purple. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n4\tYou have chosen rightly\tThe lockbox is in Signoth's estate in Edoras. You should open the lockbox by choosing the correct colour. NOTE: From left to right, the gems are Blue, Green, Red, Purple. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n5\tCompleted\tYou have opened the lockbox!\n",
[4568]="700399B0\n1\tSpeak with Atwald at your side\tAtwald is at your side. You should speak with Atwald.\n2\tDemonstrate to Atwald how you may help in Edoras\tSurely there is someone near the tavern area who is in need of assistance before the journey. You should assist someone who is readying themselves to leave for Dunharrow, with Atwald at your side.\n3\tSpeak with Atwald at your side\tAtwald is at your side. You should speak with Atwald.\n4\tCompleted\tYou have hopefully turned the tide of sadness in Edoras by inspiring Atwald, for the people are in great need of cheering.\n",
[4569]="70039761\n1\tGift your catch to Dúdrad\tDúdrad's fishing area can be found where the river meets the road, just outside of the south-west wall of Edoras. You should gift your catch to Dúdrad.\n",
[4570]="70039760\n1\tEncourage Sigun to leave\030Encourage Sigmar to leave\tThe quarrelling brothers Sigmar and Sigun can be found outside their late father's estate atop a hill near the fountain north of Meduseld. You should speak with each of the quarrelling brothers.\n2\tReturn to Britred\tBritred can be found at atop the fountain wall north of Meduseld. You should return to Britred.\n3\tAsk Britred about Elfwyn\tBritred can be found atop the fountain wall north of Meduseld. You should ask Britred about the woman they mentioned, Elfwyn.\n4\tAsk Elfwyn about the brothers' dispute\tElfwyn can be found at her home just outside the market-place of Edoras, north of Meduseld. You should find Elfwyn and ask her about the quarrelling brothers.\n5\tConvince Sigmar of his folly\tThe quarrelling brothers Sigmar and Sigun can be found outside their late father's estate atop a hill near the fountain north of Meduseld. You should speak with the quarrelling brothers.\n",
[4571]="70039F10\n1\tCollect pelts from animals (total: 6)\030Collect nettles for soothing tea (total: 4)\030Collect burdock for soothing tea (total: 4)\030Speak with Atwald at your side\tBeasts and pain-soothing herbs can be found in the plains of Kingstead, especially near the river just north of the main gate. You should collect pelts from beasts, and pick some soothing herbs while you are out. NOTE: This quest must be completed alongside 'A Melancholy Minstrel,' with Atwald at your side.\n2\tSpeak with Atwald at your side\tAtwald is at your side. You should speak with Atwald. NOTE: This quest must be completed alongside 'A Melancholy Minstrel,' with Atwald at your side.\n3\tBring the goods to Céolthryth\tCéolthryth is outside of her home in north-western Edoras, near the main gate. You should speak with Céolthryth.\n4\tSpeak with Atwald once more\tAtwald is at your side. You should speak with Atwald. NOTE: This quest must be completed alongside 'A Melancholy Minstrel,' with Atwald at your side.\n5\tCompleted\tYou have inspired Atwald to be more positive, and inspire his fellow Rohirrim rather than depress them. All hearts are heavy in Edoras, and the last thing the people need is to be weighed down with more sad thoughts.\n",
[4572]="700385EC\n1\tAsk Garwold about his waggon troubles\tGarwold is in north-western Edoras, very near the main gate. You should speak with Garwold.\n2\tRepair broken waggons (total: 8)\tBroken waggons can be found in western Edoras. You should repair waggons so that the move to Dunharrow will be easier to bear.\n3\tReturn to Garwold\tGarwold is in western Edoras. You should return to Garwold.\n",
[4573]="7003A114\n1\tBake Wayfarer's Bread (total: 5)\tThe oven of eastern Edoras can be found near the eastern gate of the city. You should bake rations of Wayfarer's bread for the poorer people of Edoras.\n2\tTownspeople who are worried about food can be found throughout eastern Edoras. You should deliver the bread to townspeople without food to bring with them.\t\n3\tCompleted\tThanks to you, the hungry townspeople of Edoras now have fresh Wayfarer's Bread to sate their hunger on their journey to Dunharrow.\n",
[4574]="70015E05\n1\tDefeat half-orcs (total: 12)\tHalf-orcs can be found south-east of Gwingris. Calelloth has instructed you to go forth and defeat the half-orcs who are stealing worm-eggs for their master.\n2\tTalk to Calelloth at Gwingris\tCalelloth is at Gwingris, north-west of where you found the half-orcs. You should speak with Calelloth regarding your victory against the half-orcs.\n",
[4575]="70025B7F\n1\tSmash the salamander-eggs (total: 12)\tSalamander-nests can be found along the shoreline of Tyl Ruinen. Lúgethir asked you to find salamander-nests and smash the eggs within.\n2\tTalk to Lúgethir on Tyl Ruinen\tLúgethir is with Humphrey on Tyl Ruinen. Lúgethir will be pleased to hear you have smashed many a salamander-egg.\n",
[4576]="700032F5\n1\tPickup the egg basket\tGammer Tunnelly can be found in the centre of Tuckborough. When you returned from delivering the eggs to Holly Hornblower, he asked you to make another delivery to Gammer Tunnelly in Tuckborough. Be careful that the rooster doesn't see you with the eggs, as he will let out a call that will upset the hens. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tTalk to Farmer Sandson\tGammer Tunnelly was grateful for the eggs. You should return to Farmer Sandson and let him know the eggs were delivered without incident.\n",
})
